module

public import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute
public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Homology.DerivedCategory.RightDerivedExactFunctor
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Crystalline.SmallSite.AffineGlobalConstantSheaf
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Crystalline.SmallSite.LocalizedSiteCohomology
public import StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Sites.Cohomology.ChaoticSite.HigherDirectImageOverObjects
public import StacksFrontier.Homology.CompositeCollapse

/-!
# The higher direct images onto the chaotic subsite vanish for a sheaf satisfying Stacks 07JJ

Fix a global crystalline situation `(p, (S, I, γ), X)` of [Stacks, Tag 07MF] with `X` and `S`
affine, and let `u = wholeToAffineSubsite : 𝒞 ⥤ AffineCris(X/S)` be the inclusion of the chaotic
subsite of thickenings of the whole of `X`.  Let `f_*` be the direct image of abelian sheaves
along `u`, so that `f_* F = F|_𝒞`, and `R^p f_*` its higher direct images.

Step 4 of the proof of [Stacks, Tag 07JK] needs `R^p f_* F = 0` for `p > 0`, and reduces it, by
Cohomology on Sites, Lemma 21.7.4 — [Stacks, Tag 072W] — to the vanishing of `H^p` over the
objects of `AffineCris(X/S)`, which is [Stacks, Tag 07JJ].  This file carries out that reduction:
it takes the conclusion of [Stacks, Tag 07JJ] for an abelian sheaf `F` on `Cris(X/S)`, in the
form in which the source states it — the vanishing of the cohomology of the localized site
`Cris(X/S)/(U, T, δ)` for every object with affine ambient scheme — and produces the vanishing of
the higher direct images along `u`.

Three identifications are chained:

1. `H^p(Cris(X/S)/A, F|_A) ≅ R^p Γ(A, F)` — the localized-site bridge of
   `StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Crystalline/SmallSite/LocalizedSiteCohomology.lean`;
2. `R^p Γ(A, F) ≅ R^p Γ(B, F|_{AffineCris(X/S)})` for an affine object `A = affineι B` — the
   collapse of the derived functors of a composite along the *equivalence* `F ↦ F|_{AffineCris}`,
   which is exact and preserves injectives, so has no higher derived functors;
3. `Γ(V, R^p f_* F|_{AffineCris}) ≅ R^p Γ(u V, F|_{AffineCris})` — the chaotic case of
   [Stacks, Tag 072W],
   `Stacks.Cohomology.ChaoticSite.higherDirectImageSectionsIso`, together with the fact that a
   sheaf on a chaotic site with vanishing sections vanishes.

## Main definitions

Everything below lives in the namespace `Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.SmallSite`.

* `restrictAffineToWhole` — the restriction `F ↦ F|_𝒞` of an abelian sheaf on the affine
  crystalline site to the chaotic subsite `𝒞`, which is `f_*`.
* `higherDirectImageToWhole` — the higher direct images `R^p f_*` along that restriction.
* `Vanishing07JJ` — **the conclusion of [Stacks, Tag 07JJ]** for an abelian sheaf on the small
  crystalline site: the cohomology of the localized site `Cris(X/S)/(U, T, δ)` vanishes in
  positive degrees for every object whose ambient scheme is affine.

## Main results

* `rightDerivedSectionsAffineIso` — the derived sections over an affine object are the same
  computed on `Cris(X/S)` and on `AffineCris(X/S)`.
* `isZero_rightDerivedSections_of_vanishing07JJ` — `Vanishing07JJ` read as the vanishing of the
  right derived sections over an affine object.
* **`isZero_higherDirectImageToWhole_of_vanishing07JJ`** — **`R^p f_* F|_{AffineCris} = 0` for
  `p > 0`**, for an abelian sheaf `F` on `Cris(X/S)` satisfying `Vanishing07JJ`.

## What is and is not proved

What is proved is the reduction, not [Stacks, Tag 07JJ] itself: `Vanishing07JJ` is a hypothesis
on the abelian sheaf, and the library does not discharge it.  The fragment it has is
`Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.SmallSite.isZero_cohomology_restriction_of_isAffine`, the
vanishing of the *Zariski* cohomology of the restriction `F_T` on an affine ambient scheme `T`
for a locally quasi-coherent module `F`; passing from that to the vanishing of the crystalline
cohomology of the localized site is the Čech argument of [Stacks, Tag 03F9], which is not carried
out anywhere in the library.

No tag attribute is placed here.  [Stacks, Tag 072W] is proved only in the chaotic case, in
`StacksFrontier/CategoryTheory/Sites/Cohomology/ChaoticSite/HigherDirectImageOverObjects.lean`, and
[Stacks, Tag 07JJ] is assumed rather than proved.

`Vanishing07JJ` is stated for an abelian sheaf rather than for a locally quasi-coherent
`𝒪_{X/S}`-module.  **At that generality it is false**, and a consumer should read it as a
hypothesis to be discharged only after restricting to a module: the vanishing of `H^p` over an
affine object in positive degree is a property of locally quasi-coherent modules, not of abelian
sheaves.  The topology of `Cris(X/S)` is generated by the restriction covers of
`Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.restrictCoverage_toGrothendieck`, so an abelian sheaf
with nonvanishing Čech `H^1` on a Zariski cover of an affine ambient scheme is a counterexample.

The universe obstruction that this docstring previously gave as the reason is real but not
decisive, and the conclusion drawn from it was wrong.  A sheaf of `𝒪_{X/S}`-modules in the sense
of `Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.SmallSite.structureSheaf` has its modules in `Type u`,
so its underlying abelian sheaf lands in `AddCommGrpCat.{u}`, where sheafification on `Cris(X/S)`
is not available, while cohomology on `Cris(X/S)` exists only at the coefficient universe
`u + 1`.  But `SmallSite.abelianSheaf` of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Crystalline/SmallSite/AffineCohomology.lean` lifts the underlying
abelian sheaf to `AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1}` along `AddCommGrpCat.uliftFunctor`, which preserves
limits of every size.  So local quasi-coherence *can* appear as a hypothesis, in the form
`Vanishing07JJ S (SmallSite.abelianSheaf F)` with `F` locally quasi-coherent, and that — not the
present statement — is what a proof of [Stacks, Tag 07JJ] should establish.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 07JJ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07JJ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07JK](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07JK)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07MF](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07MF)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 072W](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/072W)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03F9](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03F9)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Abelian CategoryTheory.Limits AlgebraicGeometry Opposite
open scoped AlgebraicGeometry

universe u

noncomputable section

namespace Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.SmallSite

variable (S : GlobalCrystallineSituation.{u})

/-- **The conclusion of [Stacks, Tag 07JJ]** for an abelian sheaf `F` on the small crystalline
site: for every object `(U, T, δ)` of `Cris(X/S)` whose ambient divided power scheme `T` is
affine, and every `p > 0`, the cohomology `H^p(Cris(X/S)/(U, T, δ), F)` of the localized site
vanishes.

The source proves this for a locally quasi-coherent `𝒪_{X/S}`-module; it is carried here as a
hypothesis on an abelian sheaf, which is the only form in which it can be combined with the
cohomology of `Cris(X/S)` — see the module docstring. -/
def Vanishing07JJ (F : Sheaf (smallTopology S) AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1}) : Prop :=
  ∀ (A : CrystallineThickening S), IsAffine A.obj.thickening.target.scheme →
    ∀ p : ℕ, 0 < p → IsZero ((overCohomologyFunctor S A p).obj ((restrictToOver S A).obj F))

/-- **The right derived sections over an affine object do not change under restriction to the
affine crystalline site.**  Restriction to `AffineCris(X/S)` is an equivalence, hence exact with
no higher derived functors and preserving injective objects, so the derived functors of the
composite collapse (`Stacks.RightDerivedComp.objIso`); and the composite of the restriction with
the sections over `B` is the sections over `affineι B` on the nose. -/
def rightDerivedSectionsAffineIso (B : AffineCrystallineThickening S)
    (F : Sheaf (smallTopology S) AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1}) (p : ℕ) :
    (((sheafSections (smallTopology S) AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1}).obj
        (op ((affineι S).obj B))).rightDerived p).obj F ≅
      (((sheafSections (affineTopology S) AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1}).obj (op B)).rightDerived p).obj
        ((restrictToAffine S).obj F) :=
  Stacks.RightDerivedComp.objIso (restrictToAffine S) (injectiveResolution F)
    (fun m hm => CategoryTheory.Functor.isZero_rightDerived_of_exact (restrictToAffine S) F m hm)
    ((sheafSections (affineTopology S) AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1}).obj (op B)) p

/-- **[Stacks, Tag 07JJ] read as the vanishing of right derived sections.**  For an abelian sheaf
`F` satisfying `Vanishing07JJ`, an object `B` of `AffineCris(X/S)` and `p > 0`, the `p`-th right
derived sections of `F|_{AffineCris(X/S)}` over `B` vanish.

The localized-site cohomology of the hypothesis is turned into right derived sections over the
object by `overCohomologyIsoRightDerivedSections`, and those are transported to the affine site
by `rightDerivedSectionsAffineIso`. -/
theorem isZero_rightDerivedSections_of_vanishing07JJ
    {F : Sheaf (smallTopology S) AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1}} (hF : Vanishing07JJ S F)
    (B : AffineCrystallineThickening S) (p : ℕ) (hp : 0 < p) :
    IsZero ((((sheafSections (affineTopology S) AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1}).obj
      (op B)).rightDerived p).obj ((restrictToAffine S).obj F)) :=
  have : IsAffine ((affineι S).obj B).obj.thickening.target.scheme := B.property.2
  ((hF ((affineι S).obj B) B.property.2 p hp).of_iso
      (overCohomologyIsoRightDerivedSections S ((affineι S).obj B) F p).symm).of_iso
    (rightDerivedSectionsAffineIso S B F p).symm

variable [IsAffine S.X]

/-- **The restriction `F ↦ F|_𝒞`** of an abelian sheaf on the affine crystalline site to the
chaotic subsite `𝒞` of thickenings of the whole of `X`.  This is the direct image `f_*` of the
morphism of topoi that step 2 of the proof of [Stacks, Tag 07JK] produces. -/
abbrev restrictAffineToWhole :
    Sheaf (affineTopology S) AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1} ⥤
      Sheaf (chaoticTopology S) AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1} :=
  (wholeToAffineSubsite (S := S)).sheafPushforwardContinuous AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1}
    (chaoticTopology S) (affineTopology S)

/-- **The higher direct images `R^p f_*`** along the restriction to the chaotic subsite `𝒞`. -/
abbrev higherDirectImageToWhole (p : ℕ) :
    Sheaf (affineTopology S) AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1} ⥤
      Sheaf (chaoticTopology S) AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1} :=
  Stacks.Cohomology.HigherDirectImageDelta.higherDirectImage (chaoticTopology S)
    (affineTopology S) AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1} (wholeToAffineSubsite (S := S)) p

/-- **The higher direct images onto the chaotic subsite vanish**, `R^p f_* F|_{AffineCris} = 0`
for `p > 0`, for an abelian sheaf `F` on `Cris(X/S)` satisfying the conclusion
`Vanishing07JJ` of [Stacks, Tag 07JJ].

This is step 4 of the proof of [Stacks, Tag 07JK] minus its Leray half.  By the chaotic case of
[Stacks, Tag 072W] the sections of `R^p f_* G` over an object `V` of `𝒞` are the `p`-th right
derived sections of `G` over `u V`, and `u V` is an object of `AffineCris(X/S)`, so those vanish
by `isZero_rightDerivedSections_of_vanishing07JJ`; a sheaf on a chaotic site all of whose
sections vanish is zero. -/
theorem isZero_higherDirectImageToWhole_of_vanishing07JJ
    {F : Sheaf (smallTopology S) AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1}} (hF : Vanishing07JJ S F)
    (p : ℕ) (hp : 0 < p) :
    IsZero ((higherDirectImageToWhole S p).obj ((restrictToAffine S).obj F)) :=
  Stacks.Cohomology.ChaoticSite.isZero_higherDirectImage_of_isZero_rightDerivedSections
    (affineTopology S) AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1} (wholeToAffineSubsite (S := S))
    ((restrictToAffine S).obj F) p
    fun V => isZero_rightDerivedSections_of_vanishing07JJ S hF
      ((wholeToAffineSubsite (S := S)).obj V) p hp

end Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.SmallSite

end

end
